{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-49387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $u=1+{x}^{2}$, which integral is equivalent to $\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u=1+{x}^{2}$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,x\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n${x}^{2}=u-1$\n\nNow we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}} & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\cdot x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (u-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{1/2}-{u}^{-1/2})\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e88b9319533b4259a42088cb25d6ebdfc4e63bce2befb49c38152aa2b214913"} {"question" "q-49387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\int ({u}^{1/2}-{u}^{-1/2})\\text{d}u"] ["math" "2\\int {u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{1/2}+{u}^{-1/2})\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{1/2}-{u}^{-1/2})\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{1/2}-{u}^{-1/2})\\text{d}u"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $u=2x+1$, which integral is equivalent to $\\int x\\sqrt[3]{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u=2x+1$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x=\\frac{1}{2}(u-1).$\n\nNow we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\sqrt[3]{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(u-1)(\\sqrt[3]{u})(\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int (u-1)({u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int ({u}^{4/3}-{u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e88b9319533b4259a42088cb25d6ebdfc4e63bce2befb49c38152aa2b214913"} {"question" "q-49528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{4/3}+{u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{4/3}+{u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{5/3}-{u}^{2/3})\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\int ({u}^{1/3}-u)\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\int ({u}^{4/3}-{u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49528" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}\\int ({u}^{4/3}-{u}^{1/3})\\text{d}u"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $u=3-2{x}^{2}$, which integral is equivalent to ${\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{3-2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u=3-2{x}^{2}$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4x\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{\\text{d}u}{4}=x\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe also note that ${x}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}(3-u).$ \n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{3-2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{3-2{x}^{2}}\\cdot x\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\text{d}u}{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e88b9319533b4259a42088cb25d6ebdfc4e63bce2befb49c38152aa2b214913"} {"question" "q-49532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-49532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-346390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1/2}^{3/2}4x\\sqrt{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-346390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=2x+1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x=\\frac{1}{2}(u-1).$ \n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $-1/2$ | $3/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $0$ | $4$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{3/2}4x\\sqrt{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(u-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}({u}^{3/2}-{u}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{(5/2)}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{1}{(3/2)}{u}^{3/2})|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2})|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot {4}^{5/2}-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {4}^{3/2})-(\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot {0}^{5/2}-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{5}-\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{112}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-346390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e88b9319533b4259a42088cb25d6ebdfc4e63bce2befb49c38152aa2b214913"} {"question" "q-346390" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-346390" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{112}{15}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-346393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{6}\\frac{3x+1}{\\sqrt{x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-346393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $u=x+3.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x=u-3.$ \n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $1$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $4$ | $9$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}\\frac{3x+1}{\\sqrt{x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{4}^{9}\\frac{3(u-3)+1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{9}\\frac{3u-8}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{9}(3{u}^{1/2}-8{u}^{-1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{(3/2)}{u}^{3/2}-\\frac{8}{(1/2)}{u}^{1/2})|}_{4}^{9} \\\\  & ={(2{u}^{3/2}-16{u}^{1/2})|}_{4}^{9} \\\\  & =(2\\cdot {9}^{3/2}-16\\cdot {9}^{1/2})-(2\\cdot {4}^{3/2}-16\\cdot {4}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 27-16\\cdot 3)-(2\\cdot 8-16\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =(54-48)-(16-32) \\\\  & =6-(-16) \\\\  & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-346393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e88b9319533b4259a42088cb25d6ebdfc4e63bce2befb49c38152aa2b214913"} {"question" "q-346393" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"} {"question" "q-346393" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "22"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067660/state.json" "file_sha256" "0810f92c6aeea5bb4a6b209608e642f76d0c63330c994a57a1cbc37291435068"}] "usage" {} "basis" 22